1. Clean-Room Windows Implementation & Zero Third-Party Dependencies
===============================================================================

This project is an independent, clean-room Windows implementation developed in
Windows PowerShell (compatible with Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7+)
and native .NET Framework / Win32 platform APIs.

- Zero Bundled Third-Party Code: This repository bundles no third-party
  libraries, external binary executables, node modules, or external PowerShell
  modules.
- Zero Runtime Dependencies: All filesystem handle-bound deletion routines,
  registry queries, Win32 P/Invoke structures, cryptographic hashing, desktop
  WPF compilation, and serialization logic utilize standard built-in Windows
  platform interfaces.

===============================================================================
2. Security-First Windows Architecture & Strict Non-Goals
===============================================================================

Claude Residual ID Cleaner is purpose-built for Windows NTFS and Windows user
environments with strict fail-closed invariants:

- NTFS reparse-point protection and Windows Security Identifier (SID) tree
  ownership verification without mutating ACLs or taking ownership.
- Win32 handle-bound file disposition (SetFileInformationByHandle) and open-
  handle registry deletion (ntdll!NtDeleteKey) with zero Remove-Item fallback.
- Deterministic SchemaVersion = 3 cleanup plans with single-use SHA-256
  manifest binding and an atomic anti-replay execution ledger.
- Strict non-goals: never alters Windows OS files, system hardware/device IDs
  (such as MachineGuid), proxies, telemetry, or WSL distributions; never reads
  Credential Manager secrets or environment variable values; never claims to
  alter remote server-side account records.

